<article class="env-lemma" id="0CHK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CHK">Lemma <span data-tag="0CHK">76.48.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. A Koszul-regular immersion of algebraic spaces over $S$ is a local complete intersection morphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $i : X \to Y$ be a Koszul-regular immersion of algebraic spaces over $S$. By definition there exists a surjective étale morphism $V \to Y$ where $V$ is a scheme such that $X \times _ Y V$ is a scheme and the base change $X \times _ Y V \to V$ is a Koszul-regular immersion of schemes. By More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/069L" data-tag="069L">37.62.9</a> we see that $X \times _ Y V \to V$ is a local complete intersection morphism. From Definition <a href="/tag/06C4" data-tag="06C4">76.48.1</a> we conclude that $i$ is a local complete intersection morphism of algebraic spaces. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>